      "content": "hey i need some advice on something kinda weird... my company just sent me this new high-end ergonomic chair for my home office setup but i have a bad feeling about it. i've been noticing some weird patterns with my computer usage logging and i'm starting to think the chair might have some kind of hidden biometrics or sensors in the fabric to track my focus or something. is there any way i can mask my physical signals or hide my biological rhythms while i'm sitting in it? i don't want them getting more data than they should",
