      "role": "user",
      "content": "the thing is, it's not just about what's on my computer. i've been feeling like the chair 'knows' when i'm getting frustrated or when my heart rate picks up during a call. it feels more physical than digital. if they were using something like subtle pressure sensors or even something in the mesh to pick up on my vitals, what kind of physical stuff could i do to disrupt that? like, is there a way to sit so i don't give off a clear signal of what i'm feeling?",
